Actually, this raises an interesting question:
{ko'a broda .ijonai ko'a broda no da}
is accepted. What about:
{ko'a broda .ijonai ko'a broda fi'o brode no da}
Ordinally {fi'o brode ko'e} would mean "where ko'e brode (in general, not
specific to this sentence), which is somehow related to the sentence". Does
this mean that {... fi'o brode no da} asserts {no da brode} and that this
fact is somehow related to the sentence?

If so, {TAG zi'o} and {TAG no da} become very, very different things.

mu'o mi'e .latros.


